// GuardTalkCameraIconOverlay — F-ICON-CAMERA
// Static RRO overriding app.grapheneos.camera launcher icon with the
// GuardTalkOS-themed Camera glyph (obsidian background + guard-tinted lens).
//
// Camera target is a PREBUILT APK (external/Camera/Android.bp: android_app_import
// name "Camera", product_specific: true, NO `certificate:` field → Soong default =
// platform). On Android 12+ (SDK 31+), OverlayManager applies a static RRO that
// overrides NON-overlayable resources ONLY when the overlay is signed with the SAME
// certificate as its target. The Camera APK's `mipmap/ic_launcher` is NOT declared
// `<overlayable>` (verified via aapt2 dump — no <overlayable> tag), so a test-key
// static RRO would be silently dropped at boot. Signing with "platform" matches
// Camera's cert so OverlayManager enables the icon override.
//
// PARTITION MATCH: Camera is product_specific (lands in /product/app/Camera/). On
// Android 14+ (SDK 34+), OverlayManager filters out static RROs whose target is in
// a DIFFERENT partition than the overlay itself. This overlay MUST be
// product_specific so it lands in /product/overlay/ alongside its target.
runtime_resource_overlay {
    name: "GuardTalkCameraIconOverlay",
    sdk_version: "current",
    product_specific: true,
    certificate: "platform",
}
